Summary: I want hallucination... hallucination... SDsz3f[...

So Lazuli-T's wandering around in the DoD and quaffs a hallucination potion.
Bummer, says I; I always wind up finding a corner to hide in until it wears
off, because I can't tell friend from foe while hallucinating.  Only thing is,
I recently got hilite_pet working (figured out how to make my NetHack environ-
ment variable longer than 80 characters) so I realize I can tell my pet apart
from the rest of the Borg.  Of course, I'm still hitting him when I try to
walk into him.  Either I should still be able to displace him (not likely) or
I shouldn't be able to identify him as a pet.  What do you think?

Oh, and it doesn't seem to me that hallucinating goes as far as it could.  I
mean, you can always identify something by stepping on it or picking it up,
and a lot of the messages ("The hologram eats a newt corpse.", "You try to
push the boulder, but in vain.") reveal the true nature of the item in
question.  How about expanding hallucinative tendencies to cases like this?
(I know about distorted engravings, but that happens when you write, not read.)
For real fun, perhaps a cursed potion of hallucination, instead of working
longer, should distort everything: walls, doors, traps, staircases, you...
(Leave the floor a floor, though perhaps pop up imaginary hallucinatory
monsters.)

For a somewhat farther out idea (Far out!  Excellent.) perhaps a blessed
potion of hallucination would be useful?  You get some minor vision, or at
least a chance of one, but of course then you have to live with talking
unicorns and Klingon warships...

Also, I wish there were a peaceful flag, like the pickup flag.  When you're
pretty sure that acid blob is really the shopkeeper, or your pet, you should
be able to attempt to walk into them, not fight them, to check it out.

(Embarrassing death #10485: caught in a corner by a wererat, wereratified,
summoned help, returned to human by damage, quaffed both water potions in
hopes one was blessed.  Nope; one was cursed.  Read a scroll that turned out
to be summon monster.  Died from a grid bug while I fended off human zombies
with a wand of fire, catching a few of my rat pets in the blast.  Intrinsics:
"You had strayed", "You were unlucky", and "You were a wererat."  Just not
my day, I guess...  (:3)

